From 688a58a1cd9f7a59fce7c464e7440e0b26e258b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 94/95] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-marble: disable
 unsupported QCE

Linux 7.3 marks CRYPTO_DEV_QCE as BROKEN: the driver cannot arbitrate
access with the secure world and is slower than the CPU. No driver binds
the SoC crypto node, yet it defaults to enabled and is an interconnect
consumer, so fw_devlink keeps the qnoc-sm8450 interconnect providers
(1700000.interconnect, interconnect-1) sync_state() pending for the
whole boot. Until sync_state() the providers keep their boot-time
bandwidth floors, so DDR never reaches its low-power state in suspend
(qcom_stats ddr count stayed 0). Disable this Linux consumer on the
board; leave the remote-controlled BAM and secure-world ownership
untouched. CPU crypto remains available. Do not override BROKEN.

This mirrors the Lenovo Asphalt (SM8475) and Xiaomi Aurora (SM8650)
board changes.

Reference: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v7.3/drivers/crypto/Kconfig

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts
index faa8e2b92e0a..7576ded31886 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-marble.dts
@@ -436,6 +436,14 @@ pm8450_l4: ldo4 {
 	};
 };
 
+&crypto {
+	/*
+	 * CRYPTO_DEV_QCE is BROKEN in 7.3: no driver binds this node, which would
+	 * keep the interconnect providers' sync_state() pending.
+	 */
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
 &gpi_dma0 {
 	/*
 	 * iommus kept from sm8450.dtsi (SID 0x5b6, matches live stock): with
